From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunnymar <sunnym@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:17:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] BufferAllocator: do not shrink a large buffer in place on
 WASI

shrinkLarge frees the tail of a large buffer with UnmapPages. On WASI that is
free() of an interior pointer of a posix_memalign block, which faults in dlfree
(arrays/shrink-large-array.js). Treat WASI like Windows: report that the buffer
cannot be shrunk.

diff --git a/js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp b/js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp
index a29759e3505a..b9d1590403aa 100644
--- a/js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp
+++ b/js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp
@@ -3680,12 +3680,16 @@ void BufferAllocator::freeLarge(void* alloc) {
 
 bool BufferAllocator::shrinkLarge(LargeBuffer* buffer, size_t newBytes) {
   MOZ_ASSERT(IsLargeAllocSize(newBytes));
-#ifdef XP_WIN
+#if defined(XP_WIN) || defined(__wasi__)
   // Can't unmap part of a region mapped with VirtualAlloc on Windows.
   //
   // It is possible to decommit the physical pages so we could do that and
   // track virtual size as well as committed size. This would also allow us to
   // grow the allocation again if necessary.
+  //
+  // The same goes for WASI, where MapAlignedPages is posix_memalign and
+  // UnmapPages is free(): freeing the tail would pass free() an interior
+  // pointer of the block.
   return false;
 #else
   MOZ_ASSERT(buffer->zone() == zone);
